# ABS(-32768) and -(-32768) in INT, and the DINT equivalents.
# Implementation-defined: the result 32768 is not representable in INT, so
# this is a range overflow, listed in ed.3 annex E / ed.2 annex E as an
# error whose handling is implementer-specific (compare int_overflow).
# The records are what IronPLC does: two's-complement wrap, the value is
# unchanged. Cycle 0 is the in-range sanity check.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: x d
outputs: ax nx ad nd
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 annex E (range overflow is implementer-specific)
---
0 x=-7 d=-7                    => ax=7 nx=7 ad=7 nd=7
1 x=-32768 d=-2147483648       => ax=-32768 nx=-32768 ad=-2147483648 nd=-2147483648
